 "text": "Hi, how's life treating you? That's a neat effect of light penetration dropping off with distance. In moist media, it's even more dramatic. You can get around it with a bit of light reflection, or you can work much larger in full sunlight. You can try shot with a white pen cap, or a few inches of room light compared to mid room. Whichever you find first gives you a rough idea. Use a satin or soft paint brand for this. High gloss finishes sheen shows every tiny bump in the medium.",
